{"@type":"Service","name":"Permit and construction drawings (BCIN)","serviceType":"Building permit drawings","provider":{"@id":"https://www.renotect.ca/#business"},"areaServed":[{"@type":"City","name":"Toronto"},{"@type":"City","name":"Vaughan"},{"@type":"Place","name":"Greater Toronto Area"}],"url":"https://www.renotect.ca/services/permit-drawings-toronto/"},
{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[
{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need a permit for my renovation?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Many projects do, especially those that change the structure, add space, move or add plumbing, or change how a space is used. Cosmetic work usually does not. We tell you early which approvals your project needs."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need an architect or can a BCIN designer do my drawings?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For houses and many small buildings, the Ontario Building Code allows the drawings to be prepared by a BCIN Qualified Designer. Larger or more complex buildings require an architect."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does a building permit take in Toronto?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Review times depend on the municipality, the type of project and how complete the application is. A complete, clear drawing set helps avoid delays during the review."}}]}
